    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d576">

                <pb facs="0536" n="462" sameAs="frus:frus1865p2/pg462"/>

                <head>Mr. Seward to Mr.
                        Williams</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 7.]</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of State,</hi>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Washington,</hi></placeName>
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1865-11-06"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >November</hi> 6, 1865.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir:</hi> Your despatch of the 26th of June last, No.
                    3, has been received. In reply, I have to inform you that the President is of
                    opinion that the offender Burgevine may, upon a just conviction, be left to the
                    Chinese custody without being reclaimed by the United States representative. But
                    this is to be understood to rest upon our own voluntary consent upon the grounds
                    of national honor, and not from Chinese right under treaty stipulations.</p>
                <p>I am, sir, your obedient servant,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>WILLIAM H. SEWARD.</signed></closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p>S. <hi rendition="#small-caps">Wells Williams,</hi> Esq., <hi
                            rendition="#italic">&amp;c.,&amp;c.,&amp;c.,.</hi></p>
                </postscript>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
